{#- What the short fixed wording of work and concerns means, stated once in the system prompt of a reader shown many of
    them; its input sets `wording_explained`, and shared/work/work_progress.j2 and concern_view.j2 then print the short
    form (2026-10-12: the long form was repeated thousands of times a day). -#}
## The fixed wording in what you read
- A work "In progress" or "On hold" is carried by the assistant until every step is done, or abandoned with a reason.
- A work's steps "Still to come" are the assistant's own: it does each step itself, as part of that work.
- A concern's severity is how much it matters to the household, as the brain judged it.
- A concern's record is oldest first: a summary of the older notes, then every note since, each with when it was
  written.
- The work on a concern is one line each where the work is shown in full elsewhere: a work with a label is shown in
  full where its label is.
